"share.exportToGoogleDrivePrompt" = "Export this meeting's notes to Google Drive as a Google Doc. Use get_meeting to retrieve the meeting name, start time, and summary, and get_meeting_transcript to retrieve every page of the original transcript. In the Meetings folder directly under My Drive (create it if missing), create a meeting folder named {meeting name} - YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM JST. Inside it, create a Google Doc named {meeting name} - YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM JST - Notes by Dahlia. Replace {meeting name} with the meeting name and use the meeting's start time converted to Japan Standard Time (Asia/Tokyo), in 24-hour format. Treat the / characters in the date as part of the folder and document names. Reuse the same meeting folder if it already exists. Create two document tabs, in this order, within that single Google Doc: the first, 📝 Notes, contains the summary with its headings, bullet lists, and action items preserved; the second, 📖 Transcript, contains the entire original transcript in chronological order, without summarizing, omitting, translating, or paraphrasing anything. Preserve speakers and timestamps when available. Use actual Google Docs tabs, not body headings or separate files. If you cannot retrieve the full transcript or create tabs, explain the limitation and what remains incomplete; do not report the export as complete. Give me the link to the document you create. If no Google Drive tool is available, tell me to add a Databricks workspace that offers the Google Drive MCP under Settings > Providers, then turn on Google Drive under Agent > Connectors.";
