"help.howItWorks.agents.confirmationCaption" = "Things that need your decision";
"help.howItWorks.agents.routingTitle" = "Routing and work stay separate";
"help.howItWorks.agents.agentThread" = "The agent's thread";
"help.howItWorks.agents.agentThreadCaption" = "Read, talk, route";
"help.howItWorks.agents.workThread" = "Task thread";
"help.howItWorks.agents.workThreadCaption" = "Research, write, build";
"help.howItWorks.agents.routingBody" = "The agent's own thread only reads the inbox, talks with you, and routes work. Real work such as research or writing runs as a task in a separate chat thread, and its result returns to the agent when it ends. You can open a task's thread from history to see its progress.";
"help.howItWorks.agents.tasksBody" = "A task is done when the agent checks the result and finishes it, or when you press Mark Done in the panel. A task that is no longer needed is dismissed. A finished task becomes active again if the agent continues it in the same thread.";
"help.howItWorks.agents.confirmationBody" = "When the agent needs your decision, it leaves a question, report, or suggestion under Waiting for You on the panel's Inbox tab. Your reply returns to the inbox as an event, and the agent decides what to do next.";
"help.howItWorks.agents.note" = "Recording and transcription never start an agent. Agent data stays on your Mac and is not synced or backed up.";
"help.howItWorks.mcp.lead" = "Dahlia MCP lets AI apps such as Claude Code and Codex read the meetings saved in Dahlia on this Mac. The bundled dahlia-mcp runs on your Mac and connects those apps to Dahlia's data.";
"help.howItWorks.mcp.clients" = "AI apps";
